<style>
#form-ID-container {
	container-type: inline-size;
}
#form-ID {
	grid-template-areas:
		'siteName'
		'env'
		'timezone'
		'section-divider-1'
		'notfound'
		'maxDownloadSize'
		'section-divider-2'
		'appLogLevel'
		'sentry';
	grid-template-columns: 1fr;
}
@container (min-width: 500px) {
	#form-ID {
		grid-template-areas:
			'siteName'
			'env'
			'timezone'
			'section-divider-1 '
			'notfound'
			'maxDownloadSize'
			'section-divider-2 '
			'appLogLevel'
			'sentry';
		grid-template-columns: repeat(1, 1fr);
	}
}
</style><div id="form-ID-container"><form id="form-ID" class="totalform help-on-hover help-box formgrid" data-method="POST" data-route="/admin/settings/general"><hr class="form-grid-section-divider" style="grid-area: section-divider-1;"/><hr class="form-grid-section-divider" style="grid-area: section-divider-2;"/><div class="form-field text-field " data-type="text" style="--grid-area: siteName;"><label for="field-UID">Site Name</label><div class="form-group"><input type="text" id="field-UID" name="siteName" placeholder="Joe&#039;s Bistro" aria-describedby="help-UID" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Human-readable name for your site (e.g. 'Joe's Bistro'). Used in the MCP server identity, the <code>site_info</code> MCP tool, and other public-facing surfaces as they adopt it. When blank, T3 falls back to the admin dashboard title and then the domain.</p></div><div class="form-field select-field " data-type="select" style="--grid-area: env;"><label for="field-UID">Site Environment</label><div class="form-group"><select id="field-UID" name="env" aria-describedby="help-UID"><option value="prod">Production</option><option value="dev">Development</option></select><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Production protects live visitors and auto-disables repeatedly crashing extensions. Development surfaces extension errors loudly and never auto-disables. Overridden when an APP_ENV environment variable is set.</p></div><div class="form-field select-field " data-type="select" style="--grid-area: timezone;" data-settings="{&quot;timezoneOptions&quot;:true}"><label for="field-UID">Timezone</label><div class="form-group"><select id="field-UID" name="timezone" aria-describedby="help-UID">TIMEZONES</select><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">The timezone that all dates in the CMS will be saved as. If not set, then the default timezone that the server is configured with will be used.</p></div><div class="form-field text-field " data-type="text" style="--grid-area: notfound;"><label for="field-UID">404 - Page Not Found Path</label><div class="form-group"><input type="text" id="field-UID" name="notfound" placeholder="/404" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="/404" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">The path to the 404 page that will be used when a page is not found. This is used by the CMS to redirect when an object is not found.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: maxDownloadSize;"><label for="field-UID">Max URL Download Size (MB)</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="maxDownloadSize" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="2048" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="2048" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">The maximum file size in megabytes allowed when downloading files from a URL. This protects your server from downloading excessively large files. Set to 0 for unlimited.</p></div><div class="form-field select-field " data-type="select" style="--grid-area: appLogLevel;"><label for="field-UID">App Log Level</label><div class="form-group"><select id="field-UID" name="appLogLevel" aria-describedby="help-UID"><option value="debug">Debug</option><option value="info" selected>Info</option><option value="notice">Notice</option><option value="warning">Warning</option><option value="error">Error</option><option value="critical">Critical</option><option value="alert">Alert</option><option value="emergency">Emergency</option></select><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Minimum severity written to <code>logs/totalcms.log</code>. Lower levels are more verbose. PSR-3 levels in ascending severity: debug, info, notice, warning, error, critical, alert, emergency.</p></div><div class="form-field toggle-field " data-type="toggle" style="--grid-area: sentry;"><label for="field-UID">Share Application Errors with Developer</label><div class="form-group"><div class="switch"><input id="field-UID" name="sentry" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="help-UID"/><label for="field-UID" aria-hidden="true">Share Application Errors with Developer</label></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">In the case any critical errors happen in Total CMS, the details of the error will be shared with the developer so that a fix can be shipped as soon as possible. No private data is ever shared or stored. Only the error and where the error occurred in the code will be shared. If disabled, errors will only be logged locally on your server.</p></div><div class="form-inline-fields"><button type="submit" class="button btn cms-save cms-button">Save Settings</button></div></form></div>